omy of the patellofemoral joint</article-title><source>Knee Surgery, Sports Traumatology, Arthroscopy</source><year>2006</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>240</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00167-005-0683-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amis</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Current concepts on anatomy and biomechanics of patellar stability</article-title><source>Sports Medicine &#x00026; Arthroscopy Review</source><year>2007</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>48</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17505317</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/JSA.0b013e318053eb74</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shim</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Leung</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Blood Supply of the Knee Joint: A Microangiographic Study in Children and Adults</article-title><source>Clinical Orthopaedics &#x00026; Related Research</source><year>1986</year><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>125</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3522019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Dalley</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Moore KL, Dalley AF</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Lower Limb</article-title><source>Clinically Oriented Anatomy</source><year>2006</year><edition>5</edition><publisher-name>Philadelphia, PA: Lippincott Williams &#x00026; Wilkins</publisher-name><fpage>555</fpage><lpage>724</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name>